<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23076" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn -explōrātus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unexplored</i>, <i>not examined</i>,
				<i>unknown</i> (not in Cic. or Cæs.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vada,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 48, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">39, 51, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">43, 4, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inventio mihi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 6, 25, § 43</span></i>
			.— <i>Advv.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-explōrātē</span></b> ,
				<i>without examining beforehand</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non temere, nec inexplorate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					5, 19, 5</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-explō-rātō</span></b> ,
				<i>without previous examination</i> (a favorite
			word of Livy): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ibi inexplorato profectus, in insidias
					praecipitatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					21, 25, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 30, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">22, 4, 4</span></i>; 27,
			26, 6.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
